The test guarantees `len(locs) == 89` and constructs `FixedLocator(locs, nbins=12)`. In `FixedLocator.tick_values`, the loop bound comes from `step = max(int(np.ceil(len(self.locs) / self.nbins)), 1)`, so `step = ceil(89 / 12) = 8`. The loop is `for i in range(1, step):`, which iterates over 1 through 7, so the first line in the loop body executes 7 times.

